                <pb facs="0588" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg454"/>

                <head>No. 311.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pak Chung
                            Yang to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Corea</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 16, 1888</date>.
                        (Received July 17.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am in
                    receipt of advices from my country today to the effect that the Corean telegraph
                    line has been completed to Fusan, connecting with the Japanese cable at that
                    point. Hereafter we shall send our telegraphic dispatches to Seoul by this
                    route.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pak Chung
                            Yang.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
